Finger for CodeWarrior

Tested with CodeWarrior Gold 4 (MW C/C++ 68K 1.1) on System 7.6.1.

Finger.π is the project. Open it and choose Make from the Project menu.
This makes Finger, the Plug-In, next to the project. Put it in Mill's
"Mill Plug-Ins" folder.
KIT-BEGIN-REPO-ONLY
(In git and the .zip the project is a MacBinary file, Finger.π.bin; the disk
image has it as it is.)
KIT-END-REPO-ONLY

The project's settings, to make one from scratch or for a later
CodeWarrior:
- Files: Finger.c, MillGlue.c, MacOS.lib, and ANSI (2i) C.A4.68K.Lib
  (for strlen; a code resource takes the A4 libraries).
- Access Paths: the SDK folder ("::" from here), so MillPlugIn.h is found.
- Processor: 2-byte ints, 68K alignment.
- Linker: Link Single Segment.
- Project: Code Resource; File Name Finger; Resource Name Finger;
  Header Type Standard; ResType MPlg; ResID 128; Creator MiLL; Type MPlg.

The Standard header starts with a branch to main, so byte 0 is the entry.
The glue names its entry main for CodeWarrior and sets up A4 for globals.
CodeWarrior writes the 'MPlg' resource itself.

For a Plug-In of your own, copy Finger.π, then remove Finger.c and add
your own files.
